==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|obez|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|obez|lang=goh}}, {{term|obaz||fruit|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|ubatjan||fruit, produce, increase|lang=gem-pro}}, from a compound whose first element represents {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|obʰi-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|ebʰi-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|bʰi-||on, toward, from, by|lang=ine-pro}}, and whose second element is {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|at|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|ēta-||edibles, food|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|etanan||to eat|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|h₁ed-||to eat|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|en|-}} {{term|ovest||mast|lang=en}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|ovet|ōvet|lang=gml}}, {{term|avet|āvet|lang=gml}}, {{term|oft|ōft|fruit|lang=gml}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|ooft||fruits|lang=nl}}. More at {{l|en|ovest}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|lang=de|/ʔoːpst/}}
* {{audio|De-Obst.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|g=n|gen1=Obsts|gen2=Obstes|pl=-}}

# [[fruit]]
#: ''Heute esse ich nur '''Obst'''.'' - Today I only eat fruit.

